# Preview servers

Default to verifying from the repo: read the code, lint, typecheck, and use a substitute already available (tests, curl against a server **already** running in a terminal).

Start Storybook, `next dev`, or any other long-lived preview/dev server **only when the user explicitly asks**. Do not start one as a default “check the UI” step. Browser automation against a preview you just spawned is the same cost: skip it unless they asked.

If a matching server is already running, reuse that process. Do not spawn a second one.
